# Waivers for the Trivy gate in .github/workflows/docker-publish.yml.
#
# The gate fails on any CRITICAL or HIGH vulnerability that has a fixed
# version. A finding listed here does not fail it. There are no waivers today.
#
# Each waiver is three things: the ID, the reason, and an expiry date. Put the
# reason on a comment line directly above the ID, and the expiry on the ID's
# line as `exp:YYYY-MM-DD`. Trivy stops honouring the line after that date, so
# the waiver has to be looked at again rather than living for ever:
#
#   # libexample: fixed only in Debian unstable so far; Apache never calls the
#   # affected function. Remove when the trixie update lands.
#   CVE-0000-00000 exp:2026-12-31
